From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:08:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 48/75] PlaitOS: Section 4 fixes from review

- Heads-up timeout: while plait_heads_up_timeout is unset keep the stock
  heads_up_notification_decay in milliseconds (crDroid rounds it through
  whole seconds, which changes any overlay value that isn't a multiple of
  1000), use it unrounded on the ambient display too, and ignore values
  under one second so a stray 0 can't make heads-ups vanish at once
- Quick pulldown: guard isOpenQsEvent() against mQs being null before the
  QS fragment exists (the rest of the class checks it; LineageOS's
  addition didn't)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNZzm3ssZ7eH5QDg4P9AiP
---
 .../shade/QuickSettingsControllerImpl.java    | 13 ++++++++-----
 .../headsup/HeadsUpManagerImpl.java           | 19 +++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

